# Keep the working copy LF on every platform.
#
# scripts/checkVarianceJumps.js and the other checks that test page logic lift
# consts straight out of public/index.html with regexes that end in ";\n". With
# core.autocrlf on, a fresh checkout on Windows is CRLF, so those checks fail
# with "const _MONTH_ABBR not found in index.html" on a tree nobody has touched
# — and the usual fix, converting the file back to CRLF to clear a stubborn
# "M public/index.html", silently breaks them again.
#
# Git stores LF either way, so this changes nothing in history; it only stops
# the checkout from rewriting the endings the checks depend on.
public/index.html text eol=lf
scripts/*.js      text eol=lf
